# Screenshot automation

To update screenshots used in our documentation, we script shot-scraper to grab
screenshots of small chunks of our UI. This uses a QA user with minimal
permissions to projects that are benign enough to exist in public documentation.
For any place we deal with sensitive information, shot-scraper can use DOM
manipulation to replace the sensitive content.

To run, simply run:

    % make

This runs the following steps:

- Creates the auth files that will contain the session information so that
  following screenshots use an authenticated request.
- Runs shot-scraper against the YAML configuration files with all the
  screenshots to generate.

Creating the auth file will open a browser so you can log in. Log in as the
directed user. This will create a file that will be reused by shot-scraper to
generate authenticated requests to the production dashboard.

To add a screenshot, select a good element that you can target to keep the
screenshot clear and helpful. Refer to the existing screenshots and the shot-scraper
documentation for usage and help configuring.
